// Package answerwire is the answers a worker reads from nova-sprint and the
// records nova-bus and the hook keep, as table wires generated by the schema
// compiler from schemas/answer (answer.schema, token.schema, hookrec.schema):
// the sprint request, result and response, the friend cards, worker, routes,
// holders and queue answers, the member packet, the bus send-token record and
// the hook judgment record. Every other .go file here is generated: edit the
// .schema and run go generate ./pkg/answerwire, never the output.
// pkg/schemaread reads it strictly: binary wire, padded standard base64 of the
// wire, or JSON text, each refused by name when damaged.
package answerwire

//go:generate go run github.com/mas-bandwidth/schema/v2/cmd/schema@v2.5.1-0.20261017012433-9b397a277ad3 generate --lang go --out . ../../schemas/answer
